                "text": "I'm examining the input pairs of vertical segments\u2014one at columns 5 and 10 with height 2, another at columns 2 and 6 with height 4\u2014and trying to figure out how they transform into diverging lines in the output, where the slope seems tied to each segment's height.\n\nTracing the 8-lines confirms they spread outward by 1 column every 2 rows going both up and down, matching the original height. Now I'm checking the 3-lines similarly: starting at columns 2 and 6, they diverge by 1 column every 4 rows going downward, matching height 4, with overlaps resolving in favor of 6 where the two diverging lines cross.\n\nRow16 resolves to col0=8, col1=3, confirming that overlaps between the two patterns produce 6. I've got the rule down now and I'm ready to test it.",
